' --- manual: everything below this line is hand-authored; the script preserves it ---

note right of workspace_commands
The unit is generated from the workspace entity model. One submenu,
one handler per protocol verb, and the request types come from the
entity's derived protocol, so the shell surface follows the model
rather than a hand-kept list.

The two operations that are not entity verbs -- the ancestor
resolution chain and the trade-scope whitelist -- have no unit here.
Nothing calls them yet, so no hand-written unit stands in for one,
unlike ores.shell.workflow's wait command.
end note

